# Server Phase Boundary

Use this Rule when working in a WordPress root over Cursor Remote-SSH.

## Server Phase Responsibilities

Keep these tasks server-side because they depend on the running WordPress environment:

- Inspecting the WordPress root, active theme, plugins, and upload paths.
- Creating or updating WST PHP templates and shortcode-driven template files.
- Creating or updating ACF field groups, Flexible Content layouts, and content values.
- Running WP-CLI commands from the project-approved WordPress root.
- Flushing object/page caches after template, DB, content, or media changes.
- Importing files into the WordPress Media Library.
- Capturing Section or CPT handoff context after WST foundation work is complete.

Server-side ownership does not override PHP bootstrap safety. Do not edit `functions.php`. Edit `theme-functions.php` or MU plugin files only after explicit prior user confirmation for the exact change.

## Local Frontend Phase Responsibilities

Hand these tasks to the local frontend phase:

- Final CSS/SCSS implementation.
- Visual refinement after any Chrome Local Overrides spike.
- Responsive browser checks.
- Browser QA via local Playwright MCP (set up through `frontend-design-qa` `setup-playwright-mcp`) and optional project-local Playwright regression acceptance against the dev or staging URL.
- Final commits for frontend code and updated Section or CPT handoff notes.

## Handoff Rule

When server work creates or changes a WST Flexible Content Section or CPT foundation, update the matching project-local handoff document before local frontend work starts. The handoff travels with the same Git branch or PR as the code.

The handoff must include:

- Page URL.
- Template files.
- ACF field group and layout references.
- CSS hooks/classes expected by the template.
- Expected visual behavior.
- QA notes and open questions.

Use WST Builder's bundled Section handoff template at `plugins/wst-builder/handoffs/section-handoff.template.md` for Section handoffs, then store the filled handoff at the project-configured location from `PROJECT-CONTEXT.md`. Use WST Builder's bundled CPT handoff template at `plugins/wst-builder/handoffs/cpt-handoff.template.md` for CPT handoffs, then store the filled handoff at the separate project-configured CPT handoff location.

## Project Context

Do not hardcode environment facts in reusable plugin content. Read the current project's `PROJECT-CONTEXT.md` for WordPress root, theme path, WST path, Section handoff storage, CPT handoff storage, WP-CLI command, cache command, editable path policy, upload policy, and verification URLs.
